00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:49.553
- Yes.

00:07:49.553 --> 00:07:51.690
And then make him do his boom operator.

00:07:51.690 --> 00:07:52.770
- He does a great
- Boom operator.

00:07:52.770 --> 00:07:53.607
He does a great boom operator.

00:07:53.607 --> 00:07:54.810
- And he does a great Muppet.

00:07:54.810 --> 00:07:55.643
- [Kelly] Those are random gifts.

00:07:55.643 --> 00:07:56.760
- Oh he does a really good Muppet.

00:07:56.760 --> 00:07:58.350
- That's random talents.

00:07:58.350 --> 00:07:59.400
I cannot wait to meet him.

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:00.420
- I know.

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:02.820
John right now is like, thanks ladies.

00:08:02.820 --> 00:08:03.653
All my bits.

00:08:03.653 --> 00:08:04.773
- You actually, you found

00:08:04.773 --> 00:08:06.840
it was from your first table read, right?

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:08.280
You found a photo from
your first table read

00:08:08.280 --> 00:08:09.214
that you all did.

00:08:09.214 --> 00:08:10.047
- Oh yes, yes.

00:08:10.047 --> 00:08:12.270
- Yes, our casting director, Allison Jones

00:08:12.270 --> 00:08:14.910
brought her camera and
she took a Polaroid of us

00:08:14.910 --> 00:08:16.230
and she gave one to each of us

00:08:16.230 --> 00:08:17.940
and I saved mine all these years.

00:08:17.940 --> 00:08:19.080
- That's so cool.

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:20.430
We do Polaroids on this show, I love it.

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:21.720
It just looks vintage and cool.

00:08:21.720 --> 00:08:24.060
- I didn't get one 'cause
I wasn't there that day.

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:25.020
- She hadn't been cast yet.

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:26.100
- I hadn't been cast yet.

00:08:26.100 --> 00:08:26.933
- Yeah.

00:08:27.930 --> 00:08:28.770
- I'm okay with it.

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:29.850
- Wasn't it funny though?

00:08:29.850 --> 00:08:31.410
Aren't you, Angela, you tried out right,

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:32.243
when everyone auditioned.
- I did.

00:08:32.243 --> 00:08:33.600
- You auditioned for her part, right?

00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:35.515
- I auditioned for the role of Pam

00:08:35.515 --> 00:08:39.840
and I went in, you guys, and
I thought I did so great.

00:08:39.840 --> 00:08:41.310
And it was a big room.

00:08:41.310 --> 00:08:42.430
- You did, you got the
job, just a different one.

00:08:42.430 --> 00:08:43.680
- Well, I got a different job,

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:45.600
but it was a room full of people.

00:08:45.600 --> 00:08:50.340
And there's a moment where
Michael is fake firing Pam

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:52.950
in front of Ryan, the
temp, to like pull a prank

00:08:52.950 --> 00:08:56.730
and Pam starts to cry
and calls him a jerk.

00:08:56.730 --> 00:08:59.880
And I called him like a jerk
and everyone started laughing

00:08:59.880 --> 00:09:00.713
and I was like,

00:09:00.713 --> 00:09:03.150
I don't think that was
supposed to be a laugh.

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:04.874
I think I missed something.

00:09:04.874 --> 00:09:08.070
And then of course you see this
vulnerable moment that Pam,

00:09:08.070 --> 00:09:10.200
as much as she hates
that job, she needs it.

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:12.900
And Jenna did such an
amazing job portraying that.

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:14.370
But so, they said I didn't get the part

00:09:14.370 --> 00:09:16.030
'cause I was a little too feisty.

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:17.626
Too feisty for Pam.

00:09:17.626 --> 00:09:18.900
- You were raised in
Texas, so it's understood.

00:09:18.900 --> 00:09:20.682
- I know, listen, I'll call someone a jerk

00:09:20.682 --> 00:09:21.515
if they're a jerk.

00:09:21.515 --> 00:09:22.860
- I'll call someone something else, yeah.

00:09:22.860 --> 00:09:24.240
- [Angela] Maybe, yeah.

00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:25.710
- It depends on the moment.

00:09:25.710 --> 00:09:26.700
- But then they brought me back.

00:09:26.700 --> 00:09:29.460
They said, hey, we've got
kind of a judgey snarky lady

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:30.333
in accounting.

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:32.370
I said, okay.

00:09:32.370 --> 00:09:33.420
- That call's amazing.

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:35.160
Hey, you know what you'd be perfect for?

00:09:35.160 --> 00:09:36.813
- A snarky lady.

00:09:36.813 --> 00:09:38.010
- This snarky lady.

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:40.260
Okay, no, but have your
kids seen "The Office" yet?

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:41.093
Do they watch it right now?

00:09:41.093 --> 00:09:42.082
- Mine have not.

00:09:42.082 --> 00:09:43.930
I have an eight-year-old
and a five-year-old.

00:09:43.930 --> 00:09:44.940
- [Kelly] Okay, okay.

00:09:44.940 --> 00:09:46.680
- And my kids hadn't seen it either.

00:09:46.680 --> 00:09:48.750
Except this year, they're in fifth grade.

00:09:48.750 --> 00:09:49.830
Two of them are in fifth grade

00:09:49.830 --> 00:09:52.170
and all their friends
watched it over the summer.

00:09:52.170 --> 00:09:54.427
And so my mom was like, I
mean, my daughter was like,

00:09:54.427 --> 00:09:57.060
"Mom, can I please finally
watch "The Office?"

00:09:57.060 --> 00:09:58.560
And I was like, okay.

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:01.890
And I was at the time watching
Healthcare for the podcast,

00:10:01.890 --> 00:10:03.510
I was like, why don't
you watch Healthcare?

00:10:03.510 --> 00:10:06.989
And she was like, "Mom,
what's an anal fissure?"

00:10:06.989 --> 00:10:09.030
(audience laughing)

00:10:09.030 --> 00:10:11.864
- Oh my God, I love this conversation.

00:10:11.864 --> 00:10:13.380
- [Angela] And I was like, I was like.

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:15.000
- Is that when you say go ask your dad?

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:17.490
- Well no, I was like, it's a real.

00:10:17.490 --> 00:10:18.630
And she goes, "Is that real?"

00:10:18.630 --> 00:10:19.893
I was like, yes.

00:10:20.790 --> 00:10:21.630
Fast forward.

00:10:21.630 --> 00:10:23.400
So I don't know, so yeah.

00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:25.020
She's watching "The Office" now.

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:26.643
It's not all anal fissures.

00:10:26.643 --> 00:10:28.646
(Kelly laughing)

00:10:28.646 --> 00:10:30.030
- It's not.
- It's not.

00:10:30.030 --> 00:10:32.610
- So out of all, it's not.

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:33.900
So out of all the episodes,

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:37.710
what scene was for each of
you was the hardest to shoot?

00:10:37.710 --> 00:10:38.543
- Oh.

00:10:38.543 --> 00:10:39.376
- We were talking about this

00:10:39.376 --> 00:10:41.430
because I mean there's hardest,

00:10:41.430 --> 00:10:44.070
emotionally hardest because
we were laughing so hard.

00:10:44.070 --> 00:10:45.052
So where should we start?

00:10:45.052 --> 00:10:46.620
- I think our hardest because
we were laughing so hard

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:48.000
was the dinner party episode.

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:48.833
- Yeah, so hard.

00:10:48.833 --> 00:10:50.820
- We just laughed our
way through that week

00:10:50.820 --> 00:10:53.583
that we ruined so many takes,
the bunch of us on that.

00:10:54.510 --> 00:10:57.990
But then hardest emotionally
was just the whole episode

00:10:57.990 --> 00:10:58.907
where we were saying goodbye

00:10:58.907 --> 00:10:59.910
to Steve.
- To Steve.

00:10:59.910 --> 00:11:02.760
- When we sing to him,
when I had my, I mean,

00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:04.890
we just were crying through everything.

00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:07.804
And when I had my goodbye
to him at the airport,

00:11:07.804 --> 00:11:09.900
that was really rough.

00:11:09.900 --> 00:11:11.940
- Yeah, we were just so teary all week

00:11:11.940 --> 00:11:14.220
and Will Ferrell was
a guest star that week

00:11:14.220 --> 00:11:16.290
and I was standing next to him for a scene

00:11:16.290 --> 00:11:19.860
and he goes "I feel like
I'm at like a funeral,

00:11:19.860 --> 00:11:22.110
but I'm supposed to be
funny at the funeral."

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:22.943
- Oh my gosh.

00:11:22.943 --> 00:11:24.930
- And I was like, oh,
that must be really hard.

00:11:24.930 --> 00:11:26.610
- Yeah.
- To be around all of us.

00:11:26.610 --> 00:11:29.610
But yeah, and then also like
there was awkward things

00:11:29.610 --> 00:11:30.780
that were hard 'cause they were awkward.

00:11:30.780 --> 00:11:34.170
Like I had to toss a cat into a ceiling.

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:36.407
- [Kelly] You really did
toss a cat like a real cat?

00:11:36.407 --> 00:11:38.310
- [Angela] I mean look at that.

00:11:38.310 --> 00:11:40.217
Oh no, it was, it was, it was all.

00:11:40.217 --> 00:11:41.490
- I mean I remember the,

00:11:41.490 --> 00:11:43.500
I thought maybe it was a fake cat.

00:11:43.500 --> 00:11:44.333
- Oh well there was a--

00:11:44.333 --> 00:11:45.570
- Parts of it were fake.

00:11:45.570 --> 00:11:47.490
- Not, well, not part of the animal.

00:11:47.490 --> 00:11:50.610
- No, but I mean parts of the
shot were with a fake cat.

00:11:50.610 --> 00:11:51.443
- And yes.

00:11:51.443 --> 00:11:53.880
But I had to like in the scene where

00:11:53.880 --> 00:11:56.730
like everyone's going crazy
and like Kevin has a copier

00:11:56.730 --> 00:11:57.690
and he's like, ah!

00:11:57.690 --> 00:12:00.180
I had to like take a cat out of a drawer,

00:12:00.180 --> 00:12:02.040
which I guess my character's
kept a cat in her drawer

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:02.873
all these years.

00:12:02.873 --> 00:12:03.810
- So that's not creepy at all.

00:12:03.810 --> 00:12:04.643
- That's not creepy.

00:12:04.643 --> 00:12:06.330
And the cat is huge.

00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:08.250
This wasn't like a little cat.

00:12:08.250 --> 00:12:09.360
It was like enormous.

00:12:09.360 --> 00:12:10.193
- Like a heifer.

00:12:10.193 --> 00:12:11.026
- It was!

00:12:11.026 --> 00:12:12.510
It was like a heifer.

00:12:12.510 --> 00:12:13.380
Bless her heart.

00:12:13.380 --> 00:12:14.213
- [Kelly] Bless her heart.

00:12:14.213 --> 00:12:15.660
- Bless her heart, she's a heifer.

00:12:15.660 --> 00:12:17.130
Anyway so I had to get this big cat

00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:19.440
and then I had to like swing it

00:12:19.440 --> 00:12:20.580
and do this whole thing.

00:12:20.580 --> 00:12:21.510
- And you're little.

00:12:21.510 --> 00:12:22.380
- And I'm little.

00:12:22.380 --> 00:12:24.338
And it's like, (imitating meows)

00:12:24.338 --> 00:12:26.174
it was like not into it.

00:12:26.174 --> 00:12:29.580
And then everyone was screaming,
so that was difficult.

00:12:29.580 --> 00:12:30.450
- Or awesome.

00:12:30.450 --> 00:12:31.770
- [Angela] Or awesome, yeah.

00:12:31.770 --> 00:12:33.150
- So "The Office" is coming

00:12:33.150 --> 00:12:35.100
to the NBC streaming service right now.

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:36.420
So would you do a reboot?

00:12:36.420 --> 00:12:37.650
Would y'all do it?

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:39.030
- We talk about this all the time.

00:12:39.030 --> 00:12:41.396
We wanna do a reunion special,

00:12:41.396 --> 00:12:44.280
like a reason that everyone in the office

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:46.320
has to reunite for some reason,

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:48.000
like a one time special episode.

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:48.833
- Like a movie.

00:12:48.833 --> 00:12:50.430
Like a reunion movie.
- Like a movie.

00:12:50.430 --> 00:12:52.230
Because I think a reboot would be hard.

00:12:52.230 --> 00:12:54.540
I think it at the end of the series,

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:55.590
I mean spoiler alert

00:12:55.590 --> 00:12:56.970
for anyone who's still
in the middle of it,

00:12:56.970 --> 00:12:59.370
but some of the people
don't end up staying

00:12:59.370 --> 00:13:00.960
at the paper company anymore.

00:13:00.960 --> 00:13:01.793
- Yeah.

00:13:01.793 --> 00:13:02.640
- They move on, they move away.

00:13:02.640 --> 00:13:04.350
And so to manufacture some reason

00:13:04.350 --> 00:13:06.780
why we're all working there
again, I think would be odd.

00:13:06.780 --> 00:13:07.613
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:13:07.613 --> 00:13:09.420
- But I think there is a reason
that we could all reunite

00:13:09.420 --> 00:13:10.260
in some other way.

00:13:10.260 --> 00:13:11.250
So that's what we're.

00:13:11.250 --> 00:13:12.083
- We have some ideas.

00:13:12.083 --> 00:13:13.020
- That's what we want, call us.

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:15.210
- Call us NBC, email us.

00:13:15.210 --> 00:13:16.050
- I think it would be so good.

00:13:16.050 --> 00:13:18.330
Like I said, like, it's
just got such a new life.

00:13:18.330 --> 00:13:20.130
Like people are like a younger age

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:21.270
are getting into these characters.

00:13:21.270 --> 00:13:22.290
It's really cool.

00:13:22.290 --> 00:13:23.550
- And on a selfish level,

00:13:23.550 --> 00:13:25.200
I would like to work with
all those people again.

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:26.850
I'd like to have us
all in a room together.

00:13:26.850 --> 00:13:27.693
- Yes!

00:13:27.693 --> 00:13:29.340
- It was such a great
chemistry, great vibe, yeah.

00:13:29.340 --> 00:13:31.830
- I teared up when I got here
because your security guy,

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:33.930
Joseph outside did
security for "The Office"

00:13:33.930 --> 00:13:34.989
for seven years.

00:13:34.989 --> 00:13:36.440
We saw him every day.

00:13:36.440 --> 00:13:37.800
- We gave Joseph a big hug.

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:38.633
- We gave him a big hug.

00:13:38.633 --> 00:13:41.400
He used to help me when
my daughter came to set.

00:13:41.400 --> 00:13:43.710
I had like a little, you
know, the little pink car

00:13:43.710 --> 00:13:45.900
you push your kid around
in and it's really loud

00:13:45.900 --> 00:13:46.890
it's like clack, clack, clack, clack.

00:13:46.890 --> 00:13:48.510
- Yeah, and everyone loves you.

00:13:48.510 --> 00:13:49.350
- Everyone loves you.

00:13:49.350 --> 00:13:50.370
I would like push her around

00:13:50.370 --> 00:13:52.980
and Joseph would like help me
take it out and set it out.

00:13:52.980 --> 00:13:54.330
And he's just a sweetheart,

00:13:54.330 --> 00:13:56.520
but I would love to see everyone again.

00:13:56.520 --> 00:13:57.409
- It would be amazing.

00:13:57.409 --> 00:13:59.670
- We might have to steal Joseph
for that week of shooting

00:13:59.670 --> 00:14:00.533
if you don't mind.
- It's okay,

00:14:00.533 --> 00:14:01.457
I'm okay with that.

00:14:01.457 --> 00:14:02.290
- We wanna come back.

00:14:02.290 --> 00:14:04.200
- Joseph can go, just so I can see it.

00:14:04.200 --> 00:14:05.033
In "The Office" though,

00:14:05.033 --> 00:14:06.840
your character punched a hole in the wall

00:14:06.840 --> 00:14:08.700
and I wanted to ask you this, like,

00:14:08.700 --> 00:14:11.430
'cause I've been able
to in a video of mine,

00:14:11.430 --> 00:14:12.360
I think it was the "Since
U Been Gone" video,

00:14:12.360 --> 00:14:15.450
I got to trash a room and they
said I could break a table

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:16.980
and it was a glass table.

00:14:16.980 --> 00:14:18.990
And then I found out,
oh, it's sugar glass.

00:14:18.990 --> 00:14:19.823
- Oh yeah.

00:14:19.823 --> 00:14:21.090
- So it wasn't really like
breaking a real glass table.

00:14:21.090 --> 00:14:22.440
It was like sugar glass,
but you feel powerful.

00:14:22.440 --> 00:14:23.273
- Yeah, oh yeah.

00:14:23.273 --> 00:14:25.200
- Were you really punching the wall?

00:14:25.200 --> 00:14:26.520
And did you break your knuckles?

00:14:26.520 --> 00:14:28.110
- Here's the thing.

00:14:28.110 --> 00:14:31.230
If you know me, you know
I'm an incredibly tough guy.

00:14:31.230 --> 00:14:32.063
- Totally.

00:14:32.063 --> 00:14:34.740
- So what I did is I told the stunt guys

00:14:34.740 --> 00:14:37.710
make that wall extra thick

00:14:37.710 --> 00:14:39.960
because I don't want it to be easy.

00:14:39.960 --> 00:14:41.760
I want, (laughs)

00:14:41.760 --> 00:14:42.788
this is so the opposite.

00:14:42.788 --> 00:14:43.621
- [Kelly] I'm powerful.

00:14:43.621 --> 00:14:44.454
- This is so the opposite.

00:14:44.454 --> 00:14:46.350
No, I was literally like, guys,

00:14:46.350 --> 00:14:47.910
we're gonna have to do
a lot of takes of this.

00:14:47.910 --> 00:14:50.382
So just make sure it's
like basically paper thin.

00:14:50.382 --> 00:14:51.215
- Yeah.

00:14:51.215 --> 00:14:53.940
- And even still, the stunt guys,

00:14:53.940 --> 00:14:56.340
like when you do something
like that, I mean,

00:14:56.340 --> 00:14:58.350
I wouldn't have thought
that's a stunt, but it is.

00:14:58.350 --> 00:14:59.670
The stunt coordinators come in.

00:14:59.670 --> 00:15:00.690
They're like, okay, here's how,

00:15:00.690 --> 00:15:01.950
we're gonna rehearse it slow.

00:15:01.950 --> 00:15:04.350
They put a pad behind the
wall, it's a whole thing.

00:15:04.350 --> 00:15:05.183
- Yeah.

00:15:05.183 --> 00:15:08.585
- And thankfully I got
through multiple takes

00:15:08.585 --> 00:15:13.170
with no serious injuries, but Kelly,

00:15:13.170 --> 00:15:17.010
I did get some scratches on my knuckles.

00:15:17.010 --> 00:15:22.010
And you know, I was cool about
it, but I got some scratches.

00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:24.990
I'm just saying.

00:15:24.990 --> 00:15:25.964
- I love it.

00:15:25.964 --> 00:15:27.450
I freaked out.

00:15:27.450 --> 00:15:29.100
I actually, I love the fact
that I got to trash a room,

00:15:29.100 --> 00:15:31.380
but then I was kinda like
you're trashing a room.

00:15:31.380 --> 00:15:32.213
I don't know.

00:15:32.213 --> 00:15:33.330
It's everything you've been told not to do

00:15:33.330 --> 00:15:34.380
like when you're kid, so you're like,

00:15:34.380 --> 00:15:35.880
I can't imagine that like,

00:15:35.880 --> 00:15:37.597
is this gonna hurt the first
punch you did into the wall?

00:15:37.597 --> 00:15:38.973
- Yeah.
- No, thank you.

